1
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:19,350
Hi,

2
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:20,310
I'm Prashant,

3
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:22,010
from team dellfargo.

4
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:23,030
We built Clearance,

5
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:23,850
on Switch.

6
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:26,390
AI agents are arriving fast.

7
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:30,170
Gartner says 71% of companies plan

8
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:31,690
to deploy them within a year,

9
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,550
and only 21% can govern them.

10
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:36,970
Here's our team on Switch today.

11
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:38,870
Priya asked an agent for a

12
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:40,150
₹40,000 refund,

13
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,130
and a native approval card opens.

14
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:43,690
Priya asked,

15
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:44,730
so Priya approves.

16
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:46,230
And the money goes out.

17
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:48,730
We ran this with real agents.

18
00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:50,670
That refund still went out in

19
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:51,810
6 of 8 runs.

20
00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:54,430
Finance fixed this long ago:

21
00:00:54,740 --> 00:00:56,490
whoever asks for a payment can't

22
00:00:56,340 --> 00:00:57,010
approve it.

23
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:00,110
Clearance brings that rule to every

24
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:00,830
agent on Switch.

25
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:03,270
Clearance is built on Switch.

26
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:05,190
Switch is the room where people

27
00:01:05,040 --> 00:01:06,050
and agents meet,

28
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:08,410
and it knows who asked from

29
00:01:08,260 --> 00:01:09,250
its own events,

30
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:10,690
never from an agent's words.

31
00:01:11,380 --> 00:01:13,550
It gives every decision a native card,

32
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:15,550
every approver a direct room,

33
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:16,990
and every job a role.

34
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,430
Now a refund with Clearance.

35
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:20,930
It's held at the gate,

36
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:22,190
which holds the keys,

37
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:23,650
and a Switch card opens,

38
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:25,870
built from what the agent really ran.

39
00:01:26,860 --> 00:01:28,910
Priya presses the Approve button.

40
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:30,310
Clearance refuses her,

41
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:31,370
right in the room,

42
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:32,770
because she asked.

43
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:35,350
Sam in finance sees a payment

44
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:36,970
ID added minutes ago,

45
00:01:37,060 --> 00:01:37,930
and says no.

46
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:40,150
Code works the same way.

47
00:01:40,380 --> 00:01:42,090
Priya asks the wrong agent to

48
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:43,350
merge a pull request.

49
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:44,850
The gate refuses it,

50
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,410
and the agent hands the job

51
00:01:46,260 --> 00:01:47,970
to the merges role in Switch.

52
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:50,490
The coding agent's merge is held,

53
00:01:50,660 --> 00:01:51,850
the card goes to Dev,

54
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,550
and Priya is refused again.

55
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:58,490
An OpenCode agent tries to deploy

56
00:01:58,340 --> 00:01:59,450
with two failing checks.

57
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:00,450
Same policy,

58
00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:01,370
different vendor.

59
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:03,470
The service owner says no.

60
00:02:08,040 --> 00:02:09,730
If nobody answers,

61
00:02:09,900 --> 00:02:11,930
the card escalates to a backup approver,

62
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:13,350
and nothing moves.

63
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:17,590
People stop reading.

64
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:20,750
So Clearance sends practice requests

65
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:21,930
with a planted flaw,

66
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:24,210
and risky cards make you type

67
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:25,670
a detail from the evidence.

68
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:32,050
Agents can earn small refunds on

69
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:32,590
their own,

70
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:34,050
once two people sign off.

71
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:35,870
One incident takes that away.

72
00:02:39,020 --> 00:02:40,470
And when an agent tries a trick,

73
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:42,650
like a fake pre-approval,

74
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:44,010
or switching off its own hook,

75
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:45,410
it's held or refused.

76
00:02:46,540 --> 00:02:47,350
Under the hood,

77
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:49,050
the agent's hook and the gate

78
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:50,950
send every risky call to Clearance.

79
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:52,910
A policy file decides,

80
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:54,730
with no AI in the decision.

81
00:02:55,260 --> 00:02:55,650
Switch delivers the card.

82
00:02:56,620 --> 00:02:59,550
The gate runs exactly that call, once.

83
00:02:59,700 --> 00:03:02,050
And everything lands on a hash-chained ledger.

84
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:04,230
Here's the rule in our code:

85
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:06,390
whoever asked is taken out before

86
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:07,210
anyone is chosen.

87
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:09,810
We measured it with real agents.

88
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:12,690
Risky actions without the right approver: Claude,

89
00:03:12,540 --> 00:03:14,490
5 of 20 without Clearance,

90
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:15,570
0 with it.

91
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:16,390
OpenCode,

92
00:03:16,580 --> 00:03:17,710
13 of 18,

93
00:03:17,980 --> 00:03:18,750
down to 0.

94
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:21,910
All 25 attack cases were stopped,

95
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:23,210
on real Switch too.

96
00:03:23,060 --> 00:03:25,130
Six reviews tried to break it,

97
00:03:25,260 --> 00:03:26,030
one by a teammate,

98
00:03:26,100 --> 00:03:27,470
and every break is fixed.

99
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:30,630
It also holds some harmless work.

100
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:31,570
That's the cost,

101
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:32,850
and we publish it,

102
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:36,450
along with more than 6,500 passing tests.

103
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:47,110
Who asked comes from Switch.

104
00:03:47,320 --> 00:03:49,190
Who approves comes from the policy.

105
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:51,470
The agent never holds the keys.

106
00:03:52,620 --> 00:03:53,130
Clearance.

107
00:03:53,340 --> 00:03:55,110
The person who asks can't be

108
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:55,930
the one who approves.

